WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你们制作了这档《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会深度解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室女士》。

8
00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:25.890
Hi there, everybody.
大家好。

9
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:32.470
All right, today we're going to talk about counseling, which is Season 7, Episode 2.
好了，今天我们要聊的是第七季第二集《心理咨询》。

10
00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:41.710
But first, Ange, I feel like I want to share with our podcast listeners the morning that we had getting here.
但在开始之前，安吉，我觉得我想和我们的播客听众分享一下我们今天早上来这儿的经历。

11
00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:42.350
Okay.
好的。

12
00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:47.090
We had quite the text thread going this morning.
我们今天早上在群聊里聊得可热闹了。

13
00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:48.230
It was real wonky.
简直乱套了。

14
00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:49.890
With Sam and Cassie, you and me.
有山姆、卡西，还有你和我。

15
00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.210
I've got a summer cold.
我得了夏季感冒。

16
00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:51.610
Yeah.
是啊。

17
00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:54.770
I can't believe I am congested again.
真不敢相信我又鼻塞了。

18
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:55.890
Like, I can't believe it.
真的，我简直不敢相信。

19
00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:56.870
You just kicked it.
你明明才刚好。

20
00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.730
I barely kicked it.
我还没完全好呢。

21
00:00:58.850 --> 00:00:59.710
And now it's back.
结果现在又复发了。

22
00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:03.450
This is, you know, kids going to camps, and I don't know.
你知道的，孩子们去参加夏令营什么的，我也不知道。

23
00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.270
We're bringing all the stuff home.
我们把各种病菌都带回家了。

24
00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:06.310
Jeremy McDerMs.
杰里米·麦克德姆斯。

25
00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.110
So this morning, y'all were checking in with me.
所以今天早上，你们都在关心我。

26
00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.950
You're like, Jenna, are you okay to record?
你们问我，珍娜，你还能录音吗？

27
00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:13.110
And I was like, I'm going to rally.
我说，我会振作起来的。

28
00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:14.070
I'm going to do it.
我能行。

29
00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:14.350
Yeah.
没错。

30
00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:16.270
And then Sam was like.
然后山姆说。

31
00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.530
Yeah, I was like, I don't bring enough to this podcaSt.
是啊，我说，我不能给播客拖后腿。

32
00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:19.970
I'm going to bring Food Boys name.
我要带上“食物男孩”的名字。

33
00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:21.350
Aw, Sam.
噢，山姆。

34
00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.850
And, you know, Cassie and I are looking pretty good this morning.
而且，你知道，卡西和我今天早上看起来状态不错。

35
00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:26.130
Yeah, I don't appreciate that.
是啊，我可不这么觉得。

36
00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.730
We both just finished off the donut.
我们俩刚把甜甜圈吃完。

37
00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:31.750
Oh, yeah, they have donuts in the lobby today.
噢，对，今天大厅里有甜甜圈。

38
00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:34.170
I want to point out, Jenna's almost horizontal.
我想指出的是，珍娜现在几乎是横躺着的。

39
00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:35.530
She's almost reclined.
她几乎是半躺在椅子上。

40
00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:40.790
She's pulled another chair next to her chair so she can recline.
她在自己的椅子旁边又拉了一把椅子，好让自己能躺下来。

41
00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:42.270
But listen to this.
但你们听听这个。

42
00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:45.290
So after Sam and I are both like, we're going to do it.
在山姆和我表示我们能行之后。

43
00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:46.050
We're going to rally.
我们能振作起来。

44
00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:46.810
We got it.
我们没问题的。

45
00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:50.470
I reached into my closet to grab my office lady's hoodie,
我伸手去衣柜拿我的《办公室女士》连帽衫时，

46
00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:55.310
and I sliced my finger open on a broken edge of my plastic hanger.
手指被塑料衣架的破损边缘划破了。

47
00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.170
So then I'm like, you know what?
当时我就想，你知道吗？

48
00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:58.030
It's still okay.
没关系。

49
00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:58.390
Yeah.
是啊。

50
00:01:58.490 --> 00:01:59.430
I'm still going in.
我还是要坚持去录音。

51
00:01:59.590 --> 00:01:59.730
Yeah.
是啊。

52
00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:06.310
So I'm driving in to work and driving my daughter to camp firSt.
当时我正开车去上班，先送我女儿去夏令营。

53
00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:13.510
And there was this big sort of that moment where someone cut in front of the line of cars
就在这时，突然有人强行插进车队里，

54
00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.770
that were headed toward this one exit.
大家都正排队往同一个出口走。

55
00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.810
Everything slowed down, and I had to slam on the brakes.
车流瞬间慢了下来，我不得不猛踩刹车。

56
00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:27.410
But I could tell around me that, like, there was not enough space for everybody.
但我能感觉到周围的空间根本不够大家缓冲。

57
00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:28.390
Oh, no.
噢，不。

58
00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:29.530
Did you get hit?
你被撞了吗？

59
00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:29.970
Yeah.
是的。

60
00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:30.830
Did you hear the noise?
你听到撞击声了吗？

61
00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:31.650
You got hit?
你真的被撞了？

62
00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:33.190
Did the brake noise before it?
在那之前有刹车声吗？

63
00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:34.290
Like, were you know what's going on?
就是，你知道发生了什么吗？

64
00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:35.610
You know, it wasn't that.
你知道，并不是那样。

65
00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:38.970
I just could feel, like, the time and space around me.
我只是能感觉到周围的时间和空间，

66
00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:39.450
It slows down.
变慢了。

67
00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:44.590
And I said out loud to my daughter, I said, I think we're going to be in an accident.
我当时大声对女儿说，我说，我觉得我们要出车祸了。

68
00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:47.090
And then the person behind us ran into us.
然后后面那个人就撞上了我们。

69
00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:49.930
It was a fender bender to call it an accident.
说是车祸，其实就是个小剐蹭。

70
00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:51.230
It's not really an accident.
算不上真正的事故。

71
00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:56.410
And then, of course, it's L.A., so I'm expecting this person is going to take off.
而且，毕竟是在洛杉矶，我当时以为那个人会逃逸。

72
00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:58.890
But I'm like, no way he's pulling over.
但我心想，他不可能靠边停车的。

73
00:02:59.190 --> 00:02:59.510
Yeah.
是啊。

74
00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:00.470
He pulled over.
结果他靠边停了。

75
00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:01.170
Aw.
哇。

76
00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:02.870
He gets out of his car.
他从车里走出来。

77
00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:04.230
Young guy.
是个年轻人。

78
00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:04.670
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

79
00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:05.410
So sweet.
人特别好。

80
00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:07.570
He's wearing a Vote for Pedro t-shirt.
他穿着一件印着“投票给佩德罗”的T恤。

81
00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:09.070
Oh, Napoleon Dynamite fan.
噢，是《拿破仑炸药》的粉丝。

82
00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:09.450
Yes.
没错。

83
00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:09.770
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

84
00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:10.250
Yes.
是的。

85
00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:11.770
We check my bumper.
我们检查了我的保险杠。

86
00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:14.230
Nothing to write home about.
没什么大碍。

87
00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:15.450
We're all going to be fine.
我们都没事。

88
00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.030
But here's the kicker.
但重点来了。

89
00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:19.910
Guess where he was going to go to work?
你猜他要去哪儿上班？

90
00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:20.390
Where?
去哪儿？

91
00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:23.090
The Wizarding World of Harry Potter.
哈利波特的魔法世界。

92
00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:24.930
Oh, at Universal.
噢，在环球影城那个。

93
00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:25.590
Yes.
对。

94
00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:28.530
Which we had just been to a few days ago.
我们几天前才刚去过那里。

95
00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:30.910
And I got so excited.
我当时特别兴奋。

96
00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:33.110
I was like, oh, my gosh.
我说，天哪。

97
00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:35.410
He had just moved here from Hawaii.
他刚从夏威夷搬到这里。

98
00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:42.570
He had borrowed this car from the person he's living with to drive to his job at Wizarding
他借了室友的车，正要去哈利波特的魔法世界上班，

99
00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:43.470
World of Harry Potter.
结果就发生了这种事。

100
00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:47.110
You know, they all talk in accents in the Wizarding World of Harry Potter.
你知道，在哈利波特的魔法世界里，他们说话都带着口音。

101
00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:49.430
It's very theatrical, the whole experience.
整个体验非常有戏剧感。

102
00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:53.670
And I said to him, do they make you speak in accents?
我问他，他们会要求你用口音说话吗？

103
00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:54.290
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

104
00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:57.410
And he said, no, if you have an accent, you can speak in it.
他说，不会，如果你有口音，你可以直接用你的口音说。

105
00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:03.150
But he said he does it anyway because he's an aspiring actor and he likes to do voice work.
但他又说他还是会刻意模仿，因为他是个有抱负的演员，喜欢做配音工作。

106
00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:06.250
We had a lovely chat on the side of the road.
我们在路边聊得很开心。

107
00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:08.070
And now here I am.
然后我就到这儿了。

108
00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:09.830
And he's in the lobby.
他现在就在大厅里。

109
00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:11.490
No, I'm kidding.
不，我开玩笑的。

110
00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:17.070
I love the idea that he bumped into Pam from the office and you were excited about his job.
我喜欢这个想法，他碰巧遇到了《办公室》里的帕姆，而你对他的工作很感兴趣。

111
00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:17.670
I was.
确实如此。

112
00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.150
I was like, tell me everything.
我当时就像是，快把一切都告诉我。

113
00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:23.490
No, he did end up recognizing me and I took a photo with him.
不，他最后确实认出我了，我还跟他合了影。

114
00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:29.390
So if you know this guy and he tags us, I'll try to find it.
所以如果你认识这个人，而且他标记了我们，我会试着找出来。

115
00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:30.270
I'll repost it.
我会转发的。

116
00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:36.610
But I love that you were just chatting him up on the side of the road because I would have been there for all of that.
但我喜欢你在路边跟他搭讪，因为如果我在场，我肯定也会参与其中。

117
00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.250
And then I would have been like, what are you doing today?
然后我会问，你今天打算做什么？

118
00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:40.270
I know.
我知道。

119
00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:41.890
I was like, well, I should probably go.
我当时想，好吧，我大概该走了。

120
00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:42.870
I have to go to work.
我得去上班了。

121
00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:44.410
I have to drop my daughter off at camp.
我得送我女儿去夏令营。

122
00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:44.850
Exactly.
没错。

123
00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:47.330
But we're all fine and we're here.
但我们都很好，也都在这儿了。

124
00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:49.650
I think I'm maybe good for the day.
我觉得我今天大概没问题了。

125
00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:49.990
You're good.
你没问题的。

126
00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:50.430
I don't know.
我不知道。

127
00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:51.050
Knock on wood.
敲敲木头。

128
00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:51.690
Knock on wood.
敲敲木头。

129
00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:52.590
All right.
好吧。

130
00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:54.470
That was my morning tangent.
这就是我早上的题外话。

131
00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:55.690
Should we get started?
我们要开始了吗？

132
00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:56.890
Let's do it.
开始吧。

133
00:04:57.450 --> 00:05:01.850
This episode of Counseling was written by BJ Novak and directed by Jeffrey Blitz.
这一集《心理咨询》由BJ·诺瓦克编剧，杰弗里·布里茨执导。

134
00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:03.470
And here's your summary.
这是剧情梗概。

135
00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:07.950
As a punishment for spanking Luke in front of the entire office,
因为在整个办公室面前打了卢克的屁股作为惩罚，

136
00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:12.290
Michael must complete six hour-long counseling sessions with Toby.
迈克尔必须完成六次为期一小时的托比心理咨询。

137
00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:19.270
Dwight seeks a pretty woman-style revenge on a salesman who snubbed him at the Steamtown Mall.
德怀特对一个在蒸汽镇购物中心冷落他的推销员进行了《风月俏佳人》式的报复。

138
00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:22.630
And Pam scams her way into a new job title.
帕姆则通过欺骗手段获得了一个新的职位头衔。

139
00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:26.010
I mean, in this episode, I was like, Pam, who are you?
我是说，在这一集里，我当时想，帕姆，你是谁啊？

140
00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:32.650
You know, when this happened, it was sort of like one of those controversial character moments.
你知道，当这件事发生时，这有点像那种充满争议的角色时刻。

141
00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:35.090
We got a lot of messages about it.
我们收到了很多关于此的消息。

142
00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:36.530
And we also got mail.
我们还收到了信件。

143
00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:36.910
Oh.
哦。

144
00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:37.550
So I'll read it later.
所以我稍后再读。

145
00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:37.970
Okay.
好的。

146
00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:39.750
All right.
好吧。

147
00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:41.370
Fast fact number one.
速览事实第一条。

148
00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:45.950
I mentioned that Michael has to do these counseling sessions with Toby.
我提到了迈克尔必须和托比进行这些心理咨询。

149
00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:46.390
Yeah.
是的。

150
00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:47.550
That's our A storyline.
那是我们的主线剧情。

151
00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:55.510
It's revealed at two minutes and 52 seconds that Toby has a degree in social work from Temple University.
在两分五十二秒处显示，托比拥有天普大学的社会工作学位。

152
00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:56.930
I took a picture of it.
我拍了张照片。

153
00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:58.930
He's standing so proudly by it.
他站在旁边，看起来特别自豪。

154
00:05:59.010 --> 00:05:59.850
And then it goes wonky.
然后它就歪了。

155
00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:01.130
Yes.
没错。

156
00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:07.530
Well, the shot is only two seconds long, but a lot went into getting that diploma because it is a real diploma.
虽然那个镜头只有两秒长，但为了拿到那张毕业证可是费了不少功夫，因为那是真的毕业证。

157
00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:09.490
From the actual university.
来自那所真实的大学。

158
00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:14.010
We got a letter from Raymond Betzner in Williamsburg, Virginia, that says this.
我们收到了一封来自弗吉尼亚州威廉斯堡的雷蒙德·贝茨纳的信，信上是这么写的。

159
00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:22.610
I was the associate vice president for marketing and communications at Temple University in 2010 and helped get Toby his degree.
我曾在2010年担任天普大学市场与传播副校长，并帮忙让托比拿到了学位。

160
00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:25.170
The degree is real.
这学位是真的。

161
00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:29.010
How can Toby be a graduate from Temple University?
托比怎么可能是天普大学的毕业生呢？

162
00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:33.390
Oh, well, lady, we got a bunch of mail about, like, when was this happening?
哦，女士，我们收到了很多邮件，都在问这到底是什么时候发生的？

163
00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:36.170
Was this before or after he was in the seminary?
这发生在他去神学院之前还是之后？

164
00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.790
Was it before or after he worked in advertising?
是在他做广告工作之前还是之后？

165
00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:41.130
Toby's backstory is much like Andy's.
托比的背景故事和安迪的很像。

166
00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:42.970
It's just a free fall.
简直就是一团乱麻。

167
00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:43.810
It is.
确实是。

168
00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:45.490
Raymond went on to say,
雷蒙德接着写道：

169
00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:48.890
I got an email one day from a member of the office staff.
有一天我收到了一封来自办公室员工的邮件。

170
00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:55.050
I'm retired now and no longer have access to my email, so I can't tell you who exactly it was.
我现在退休了，已经无法访问我的邮箱，所以没法告诉你具体是谁发的。

171
00:06:55.230 --> 00:07:01.190
I was told they wanted Toby to have a master's in social work from Temple University and could I make it happen?
我被告知他们想让托比拥有天普大学的社会工作硕士学位，问我能不能办到？

172
00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:03.690
And naturally, they needed it faSt.
而且理所当然地，他们需要得很快。

173
00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:05.610
Raymond goes on to say,
雷蒙德继续说道：

174
00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:09.110
If you know anything about higher education, you need to know two things.
如果你了解高等教育，你就得知道两件事。

175
00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:12.610
First, we take degrees and diplomas very seriously.
第一，我们对学位和毕业证非常重视。

176
00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:16.270
And second, higher education doesn't move quickly.
第二，高等教育机构的办事效率并不快。

177
00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.510
But I was a fan of the show.
但我当时是这部剧的粉丝。

178
00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.050
I thought it was worth a shot.
我觉得值得一试。

179
00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:24.610
It took calls to the university registrar, the university council,
我给学校教务处、校务委员会打了电话，

180
00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:29.170
and the cajoling of several others to clear the path for this to happen.
还软磨硬泡了其他人，才为这件事扫清了障碍。

181
00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:34.650
Along the way, I kept getting nervous calls from folks at the office because they needed it soon.
在此过程中，我不断接到办公室人员打来的催促电话，因为他们急需这个。

182
00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:36.250
I was trying.
我当时已经在尽力了。

183
00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:37.850
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

184
00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:39.370
Then Raymond says,
然后雷蒙德说：

185
00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:43.970
I will also admit that I tried to get a little something in return for all this effort.
我也承认，为了这些努力，我试图换取一点小小的回报。

186
00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:44.830
Oh, Raymond.
哦，雷蒙德。

187
00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:50.390
I wanted to know if Michael and Holly got together before Steve Carell leaves the show.
我想知道迈克尔和霍莉在史蒂夫·卡瑞尔离开剧组前会不会在一起。

188
00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:50.930
Raymond!
雷蒙德！

189
00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:54.450
Did they tell him?
他们告诉他了吗？

190
00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:55.870
No.
没有。

191
00:07:56.030 --> 00:08:00.630
He says the staff at the office aren't dumb and they didn't let anything out in advance.
他说办公室的工作人员并不傻，他们没有提前透露任何消息。

192
00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:04.510
I love that what he wanted was scoop on storylines.
我喜欢他想要的竟然是剧情内幕。

193
00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:04.890
Storylines.
剧情内幕。

194
00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:05.530
Exactly.
没错。

195
00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:06.670
Not a set visit.
不是去片场参观。

196
00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:07.110
Right.
对。

197
00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:09.150
Not like an autographed something.
也不是要什么亲笔签名之类的。

198
00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:11.070
Tell me about Holly and Michael.
告诉我霍莉和迈克尔的事。

199
00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:12.070
He needed to know.
他就是想知道。

200
00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:13.610
He said,
他说：

201
00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:19.250
I'm pleased to say we were able to get the diploma approved and printed and set to California.
很高兴告诉大家，我们成功获批并印制了那张毕业证书，还把它寄到了加州。

202
00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:24.210
The photo of Toby pointing to his Temple University School of Social Work diploma
托比指着他天普大学社会工作学院毕业证书的那张照片，

203
00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:27.690
was hot on Temple University's social media for weeks.
在天普大学的社交媒体上火了好几周。

204
00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:28.110
Aw.
噢。

205
00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:34.470
So, I reached out to Randy Cordray about this, Angela, and he said that the writers had originally
安吉拉，我为此联系了兰迪·科德雷，他说编剧们最初

206
00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:40.670
considered Wake Forest University for Toby, but when they inquired about getting a degree
考虑让托比毕业于维克森林大学，但当他们询问能否获得该校的

207
00:08:40.670 --> 00:08:45.070
in social work, they found out that Wake Forest does not offer a degree in social work,
社会工作学位时，发现维克森林大学并不提供社会工作学位，

208
00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:46.550
just sociology.
只有社会学学位。

209
00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:53.250
So, that's when the writers pivoted to Temple and James Carey solved the mystery for Raymond.
所以编剧们才转而选择了天普大学，而詹姆斯·凯里为雷蒙德解开了这个谜团。

210
00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:56.210
It was Phil Shea who reached out to him.
是菲尔·谢伊联系的他。

211
00:08:56.830 --> 00:09:02.090
Phil Shea sent him a prepaid FedEx envelope to send back two diplomas, and in return,
菲尔·谢伊寄给他一个预付邮资的联邦快递信封，让他寄回两张毕业证书，作为回报，

212
00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:05.210
he did send Raymond two Dunder Mifflin hats.
他确实寄给了雷蒙德两顶邓德·米夫林的帽子。

213
00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:05.990
Aw.
噢。

214
00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:09.030
So, Raymond, do you still have your Dunder Mifflin hat?
那么，雷蒙德，你还有你的邓德·米夫林帽子吗？

215
00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:11.990
Email us a photo of you with your hat.
给我们发一张你戴着帽子的照片吧。

216
00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:14.470
Please, Raymond, can we put you in Office Lady's stories?
拜托了，雷蒙德，我们可以把你发到《办公室女士》的故事里吗？

217
00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:15.490
We would love it.
我们很想这样做。

218
00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:17.590
Well, I love knowing all of that.
好吧，我很喜欢了解这些信息。

219
00:09:17.810 --> 00:09:21.530
I mean, those little details always blow my mind.
我是说，这些小细节总是让我感到震惊。

220
00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:21.970
Same.
我也是。

221
00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:25.090
All right, are you ready for fast fact number two?
好了，准备好听第二个速递事实了吗？

222
00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:25.910
Yes.
准备好了。

223
00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:31.410
All right, this one is a little detail from Pam's storyline of trying to get her new job.
好的，这是一个关于帕姆努力找新工作这一剧情的小细节。

224
00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:33.730
We got a lot of mail from folks in Australia.
我们收到了很多来自澳大利亚观众的来信。

225
00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:36.250
Oh, yeah, because she talks about Canberra.
噢，是的，因为她提到了堪培拉。

226
00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:36.850
Yes.
没错。

227
00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:41.510
We got mail from Kimmy G in Canberra, Australia, who said,
我们收到了来自澳大利亚堪培拉的基米·G的来信，她说：

228
00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:43.230
I grew up in the Barra.
我在堪培拉长大。

229
00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:49.610
And this is just so random because Canberra is a tiny, freezing, often-missed city in Australia.
这真的很随机，因为堪培拉是澳大利亚一个很小、很冷、经常被忽略的城市。

230
00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:52.910
Most people don't even realize that it is the Australian capital.
大多数人甚至不知道它是澳大利亚的首都。

231
00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:53.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

232
00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:55.910
And then she gave this fun fact.
然后她分享了这个有趣的事实。

233
00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:57.810
Let's hear the fun fact.
让我们听听这个有趣的事实。

234
00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:03.390
The fun fact is, when they were deciding where they should put the capital of Australia,
有趣的事实是，当他们决定把澳大利亚首都设在哪里时，

235
00:10:03.730 --> 00:10:06.230
