00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:59.070
He was just so fed up.
他当时真是受够了。

471
00:20:59.210 --> 00:21:00.190
He was like, fine.
他就像是说，行吧。

472
00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:08.830
Randy also shared with me that Mike Schur, who plays Moe's, was insanely busy over at Parks and Rec,
兰迪还告诉我，饰演莫斯的迈克·舒尔当时在《公园与游憩》剧组忙得不可开交，

473
00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:12.830
and that the writers of the office would often try to put Moe's in an episode,
而《办公室》的编剧们经常想在某一集里安排莫斯出场，

474
00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:17.370
and then Randy would go check with Mike's schedule, and then he wouldn't be able to do it,
然后兰迪就会去核对迈克的档期，结果他没空，

475
00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:18.730
and they would have to take Moe's out.
他们就不得不把莫斯的戏份删掉。

476
00:21:18.850 --> 00:21:20.190
But this happened many times.
这种情况发生过很多次。

477
00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:28.090
So Randy said, finally, finally, Mike was like, yeah, my schedule's totally clear that day.
所以兰迪说，终于，终于，迈克说，好啊，我那天档期完全空着。

478
00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:31.270
I can come drop a cabbage patch to my cheSt.
我可以过来把卷心菜娃娃抱在怀里。

479
00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:34.590
Yes, and everyone was so excited because we got to have Moe's back.
没错，大家都特别兴奋，因为我们终于能让莫斯回归了。

480
00:21:35.050 --> 00:21:41.230
Well, this episode opens with Toby and Michael sitting opposite one another in the break room.
这一集开场时，托比和迈克坐在休息室里相对而坐。

481
00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:43.950
They're having a full-on stare-down.
他们正在进行一场激烈的对视。

482
00:21:44.350 --> 00:21:48.470
Michael looks like the Emperor, you know, in Star Wars when he's, like, given that death look.
迈克看起来就像《星球大战》里的皇帝，你知道的，就是那种死亡凝视。

483
00:21:48.710 --> 00:21:48.830
No?
不是吗？

484
00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:51.690
I wouldn't know that because I haven't seen those filMs.
我不知道，因为我没看过那些电影。

485
00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:53.430
I know you're thinking of Emperor Palpatine.
我知道你指的是帕尔帕廷皇帝。

486
00:21:53.530 --> 00:21:53.670
Yes.
对。

487
00:21:53.670 --> 00:21:54.430
Yes, thank you.
是的，谢谢你。

488
00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:56.730
Well, that's Michael in this opening scene.
嗯，那就是这一开场戏里的迈克。

489
00:21:56.870 --> 00:21:57.470
Thank you, Sam.
谢谢你，萨姆。

490
00:21:57.930 --> 00:21:58.810
I believe you.
我相信你。

491
00:21:59.010 --> 00:21:59.270
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

492
00:21:59.990 --> 00:22:05.670
We had a fan catch from Zach K from Acton, Ontario, Canada, who said,
我们收到了一位来自加拿大安大略省阿克顿的粉丝扎克·K的反馈，他说，

493
00:22:05.850 --> 00:22:08.030
Not really a question, but a comment.
这不算是个问题，只是个评论。

494
00:22:08.030 --> 00:22:16.050
I love how this episode begins with 15 seconds, yes, I counted it, of silence before any dialogue.
我喜欢这一集开头那15秒的沉默，没错，我数过了，在任何对话开始之前。

495
00:22:16.390 --> 00:22:20.250
This must be a record for the longest silence in the show.
这一定是全剧最长沉默纪录了。

496
00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:23.710
What's the longest silence?
最长的沉默是多久？

497
00:22:24.070 --> 00:22:25.910
27 seconds of silence.
27秒的沉默。

498
00:22:26.650 --> 00:22:28.170
Oh, with Jim and Pam.
噢，是吉姆和帕姆那次。

499
00:22:28.370 --> 00:22:29.650
On the booze cruise.
在游船派对上。

500
00:22:29.650 --> 00:22:30.230
Oh, my God.
天哪。

501
00:22:30.230 --> 00:22:31.550
I was in it.
我参与其中了。

502
00:22:31.710 --> 00:22:33.350
I was in the longeSt.
我参与的时间最长。

503
00:22:33.350 --> 00:22:34.990
I'm like, what are you talking about?
我当时心想，你在说什么呢？

504
00:22:34.990 --> 00:22:37.010
I wrote about it in a book.
我在书里写过这件事。

505
00:22:37.190 --> 00:22:37.350
Yeah.
是啊。

506
00:22:38.550 --> 00:22:40.870
Welcome to my summer cold, everyone.
欢迎来到我的夏季感冒时间，各位。

507
00:22:42.050 --> 00:22:49.090
But yes, I have to say, I thought it was a pretty badass move that the episode opens with so much silence.
但确实，我不得不说，我觉得这一集一开场就用了那么长时间的静默，真是个非常酷的举动。

508
00:22:49.690 --> 00:22:54.310
Well, I love how seriously Toby has taken this chance to help Michael.
嗯，我很喜欢托比对待这次帮助迈克尔的机会有多认真。

509
00:22:54.490 --> 00:22:56.330
He moves a small love seat.
他搬来了一个小双人沙发。

510
00:22:56.490 --> 00:22:58.510
He puts a chair in there, a little coffee table.
他在那儿放了一把椅子，还有一张小咖啡桌。

511
00:22:58.630 --> 00:23:00.730
He has a plant, a box of Kleenex.
他还有一盆植物，一盒纸巾。

512
00:23:00.730 --> 00:23:05.010
He's going to, like, get down to business and have therapy in the break room.
他打算要在休息室里认真地进行心理辅导。

513
00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:07.830
We had some fan questions about this setup.
我们收到了一些粉丝关于这个布置的问题。

514
00:23:08.070 --> 00:23:16.250
The first one's from Nicole Q from Bowie, Maryland, who would like to know, where did Toby get these sofas from for the setup?
第一个问题来自马里兰州鲍伊市的妮可·Q，她想知道，托比是从哪儿弄来这些沙发进行布置的？

515
00:23:16.550 --> 00:23:18.650
They're in the annex in the little hallway.
它们就在侧厅的小走廊里。

516
00:23:19.390 --> 00:23:22.230
Oh, I was thinking they were from front reception.
哦，我原以为它们是从前台接待处搬来的。

517
00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:28.470
Because remember, in the injury, Michael moves the couch from front reception into the conference room.
因为记得吗，在“受伤”那一集里，迈克尔把前台的沙发搬进了会议室。

518
00:23:29.090 --> 00:23:32.430
I thought they were the ones that were in the annex little lobby area.
我以为它们是侧厅小大堂里的那些。

519
00:23:32.550 --> 00:23:33.270
You're probably right.
你可能是对的。

520
00:23:33.370 --> 00:23:33.810
Closer.
再近点。

521
00:23:34.170 --> 00:23:34.650
Closer.
再近点。

522
00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:35.950
Not as big of a move.
没那么大的变动。

523
00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:37.130
Thanks, Ange.
谢了，安吉。

524
00:23:37.170 --> 00:23:37.690
You're welcome.
不客气。

525
00:23:38.110 --> 00:23:46.950
Now we have a fan catch from Emily J in Ohio, who has some comments about the little plant that you said Toby put on the table.
现在我们有一个来自俄亥俄州艾米丽·J的粉丝发现，她对你提到的托比放在桌上的那盆小植物有一些评论。

526
00:23:46.950 --> 00:23:47.870
What are the comments?
什么评论？

527
00:23:48.630 --> 00:23:59.410
Emily's theory is that the plant looks exactly like the one that died when Pam was on maternity leave, and Emily thinks maybe Toby brought it back to life just to impress Pam.
艾米丽的理论是，那盆植物看起来和帕姆休产假时死掉的那盆一模一样，艾米丽觉得托比可能是为了给帕姆留下好印象才把它救活的。

528
00:24:00.190 --> 00:24:00.710
Emily.
艾米丽。

529
00:24:02.430 --> 00:24:04.450
That is amazing.
这太绝了。

530
00:24:04.990 --> 00:24:07.550
I sort of just thought Toby took Pam's plant.
我当时只是觉得托比拿走了帕姆的植物。

531
00:24:07.910 --> 00:24:08.270
Yeah.
是啊。

532
00:24:08.470 --> 00:24:09.750
I was like, Pam, can I borrow this for today?
我当时心想，帕姆，我今天能借用一下这个吗？

533
00:24:10.210 --> 00:24:14.190
Yeah, I wasn't sure because Pam has a different plant on her desk now.
是啊，我不确定，因为帕姆现在桌上有一盆不同的植物。

534
00:24:14.330 --> 00:24:15.290
You know the one with the bow?
你知道那盆带蝴蝶结的吗？

535
00:24:15.290 --> 00:24:17.570
Oh, it looks almost like bamboo or something.
哦，它看起来几乎像是竹子之类的。

536
00:24:18.150 --> 00:24:20.850
So I don't know where this ivy plant came from.
所以我不知道这盆常春藤是从哪儿来的。

537
00:24:21.110 --> 00:24:24.050
Well, Emily, it definitely looks like a Pam plant.
嗯，艾米丽，它看起来绝对像是帕姆的植物。

538
00:24:24.350 --> 00:24:25.030
I agree.
我同意。

539
00:24:25.990 --> 00:24:31.770
Dwight is going to just burst into the bullpen, telling everyone they must boycott Steamtown Mall.
德怀特会突然冲进办公区，告诉大家他们必须抵制蒸汽镇购物中心。

540
00:24:32.370 --> 00:24:33.770
Also the kiosk.
还有那个售货亭。

541
00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:35.930
Cancel all your business with Steamtown Mall.
取消你们在蒸汽镇购物中心的所有业务。

542
00:24:36.190 --> 00:24:38.570
And then Ryan has one of my favorite lines.
然后瑞安有一句我最喜欢的台词。

543
00:24:38.790 --> 00:24:41.230
Ryan says, America is one big mall.
瑞安说，美国就是一个巨大的购物中心。

544
00:24:41.550 --> 00:24:43.190
I loved that line, too.
我也很喜欢那句台词。

545
00:24:43.190 --> 00:24:48.570
So did you know there's a mall, like, outside of New York, and you can go skiing in it?
那你知不知道纽约外面有个购物中心，你可以在里面滑雪？

546
00:24:48.790 --> 00:24:49.230
What?
什么？

547
00:24:49.450 --> 00:24:50.550
Yeah, and surfing.
是啊，还能冲浪。

548
00:24:50.990 --> 00:24:52.570
How do you ski in a mall?
你怎么在购物中心里滑雪？

549
00:24:52.850 --> 00:24:55.930
They have an indoor skiing thing.
他们有一个室内滑雪设施。

550
00:24:56.070 --> 00:25:01.450
My son found it because he loves skiing, and he is trying to find a place to ski in the summer.
我儿子发现的，因为他热爱滑雪，他正试图找个夏天能滑雪的地方。

551
00:25:02.010 --> 00:25:04.810
And he would like to ski in a mall in New York.
而且他想在纽约的一个商场里滑雪。

552
00:25:04.950 --> 00:25:06.850
If you go, will you please send me a picture?
如果你去了，能发张照片给我吗？

553
00:25:07.010 --> 00:25:07.530
Of course.
当然可以。

554
00:25:07.750 --> 00:25:08.030
Please.
拜托了。

555
00:25:08.030 --> 00:25:13.030
I feel like there's a good chance we're going to end up skiing in this mall at some point in our lives.
我觉得我们这辈子很有可能会去那个商场滑一次雪。

556
00:25:13.210 --> 00:25:14.270
I'm so curious.
我太好奇了。

557
00:25:15.170 --> 00:25:17.150
Jim wants to know, did something happen?
吉姆想知道，是不是发生了什么事？

558
00:25:17.670 --> 00:25:21.550
Andy asks Dwight for context, but Dwight tells him, you don't want to know.
安迪向德怀特询问前因后果，但德怀特告诉他，你还是别知道的好。

559
00:25:22.170 --> 00:25:22.450
Yeah.
是啊。

560
00:25:23.130 --> 00:25:29.950
Back in the therapy break room, Toby is really trying to connect with Michael, trying to get him to share about himself.
回到心理咨询休息室，托比真的在努力与迈克尔建立联系，试图让他分享自己的事情。

561
00:25:30.170 --> 00:25:35.910
And Michael is just saying a whole bunch of baloney to Toby, trying to get a rise out of him.
而迈克尔只是在对托比胡说八道，试图激怒他。

562
00:25:36.450 --> 00:25:43.050
This would have led to a series of talking heads where the bullpen shares their thoughts on Michael getting therapy.
这本会导致一系列的采访镜头，让办公室里的员工分享他们对迈克尔接受心理咨询的看法。

563
00:25:43.330 --> 00:25:44.470
Oh, please.
噢，拜托。

564
00:25:44.470 --> 00:25:47.490
In the episode, it starts with Phyllis.
在这一集中，是从菲利斯开始的。

565
00:25:47.670 --> 00:25:49.730
She says, I'm glad Michael is getting help.
她说，我很高兴迈克尔能去寻求帮助。

566
00:25:49.890 --> 00:25:52.370
He has a lot of issues, and he's stupid.
他有很多问题，而且他很蠢。

567
00:25:53.190 --> 00:25:54.890
This runner would have continued.
这个桥段本应继续下去的。

568
00:25:54.950 --> 00:25:57.070
Here are a few from the shooting draft.
这里有几个拍摄剧本里的片段。

569
00:25:57.510 --> 00:25:58.830
These were mush shoots.
这些是备选拍摄的素材。

570
00:25:59.190 --> 00:26:02.190
See if you can guess who said which talking head.
看看你们能不能猜出是谁说了哪段采访词。

571
00:26:02.350 --> 00:26:02.710
All right.
好的。

572
00:26:03.190 --> 00:26:03.970
First one up.
第一个来了。

573
00:26:04.370 --> 00:26:06.570
Sam, Cassie, Jenna, here we go.
萨姆、卡西、珍娜，我们开始吧。

574
00:26:06.690 --> 00:26:06.990
I'm ready.
我准备好了。

575
00:26:07.670 --> 00:26:09.970
Michael isn't complex enough to need therapy.
迈克尔还没复杂到需要心理咨询的地步。

576
00:26:10.230 --> 00:26:13.390
Can't someone just calmly explain to him what's wrong with him?
难道就不能有人冷静地向他解释他哪里出了问题吗？

577
00:26:15.150 --> 00:26:17.110
Oh, Oscar?
噢，是奥斯卡吗？

578
00:26:17.710 --> 00:26:18.270
Yes.
是的。

579
00:26:20.130 --> 00:26:20.890
Very nice.
非常好。

580
00:26:21.130 --> 00:26:21.250
All right.
好的。

581
00:26:21.550 --> 00:26:22.450
Next one.
下一个。

582
00:26:22.770 --> 00:26:24.510
It is high time.
是时候了。

583
00:26:24.990 --> 00:26:26.170
High time.
确实是时候了。

584
00:26:26.950 --> 00:26:27.510
Angela?
安吉拉？

585
00:26:28.330 --> 00:26:29.490
Is it you?
是你吗？

586
00:26:31.130 --> 00:26:31.690
Stanley.
斯坦利。

587
00:26:32.370 --> 00:26:32.930
Okay.
好的。

588
00:26:33.950 --> 00:26:36.230
I think that line reading was just so good.
我觉得那句台词念得太棒了。

589
00:26:36.450 --> 00:26:36.610
Yeah.
是啊。

590
00:26:37.530 --> 00:26:38.090
Okay.
好的。

591
00:26:38.350 --> 00:26:43.350
Angela does have one, and I thought rather than me reading it, let's just play it the way I said it.
安吉拉确实有一段，我觉得与其让我读出来，不如直接播放我当时录的版本。

592
00:26:44.950 --> 00:26:48.530
Talking about how many feelings you have is a form of bragging.
谈论你有多少感受是一种炫耀。

593
00:26:48.970 --> 00:26:49.870
We get it.
我们懂了。

594
00:26:49.990 --> 00:26:51.350
You have a lot of feelings.
你有很多感受。

595
00:26:51.750 --> 00:26:52.290
Whoop-de-doo.
那又怎样。

596
00:26:56.360 --> 00:26:56.820
Wow.
哇。

597
00:26:57.020 --> 00:27:00.440
She's just so put out with everyone sharing their feelings.
她对每个人都在分享自己的感受感到非常厌烦。

598
00:27:00.860 --> 00:27:03.820
And Ryan has one that comes later in the episode.
瑞安也有一段，出现在这一集的后面。

599
00:27:04.380 --> 00:27:05.680
Oh, as the tag.
噢，作为片尾彩蛋。

600
00:27:05.900 --> 00:27:06.340
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

601
00:27:06.520 --> 00:27:07.000
Yes.
是的。

602
00:27:07.560 --> 00:27:09.880
Well, we had a fan question from Sarah L.
嗯，我们收到了一位来自德克萨斯州圣安东尼奥的粉丝莎拉·L的提问，

603
00:27:10.020 --> 00:27:11.920
in San Antonio, Texas, who said,
她说，

604
00:27:12.180 --> 00:27:17.060
I would love to know if there is a backstory as to why Michael hates Toby so much.
我很想知道迈克尔为什么那么讨厌托比，这背后有什么故事吗？

605
00:27:17.060 --> 00:27:21.800
I feel like Michael has such a blind affection for his employees that there must be something
我觉得迈克尔对他员工的爱护简直到了盲目的地步，所以他讨厌托比一定有

606
00:27:21.800 --> 00:27:24.400
more to his hatred for Toby that explains it.
更深层的原因。

607
00:27:24.500 --> 00:27:28.320
Or is it just the classic angle of manager hates HR?
还是说这只是经理讨厌人力资源部的经典桥段？

608
00:27:28.920 --> 00:27:30.220
I looked into this.
我调查了一下。

609
00:27:30.560 --> 00:27:30.900
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

610
00:27:31.340 --> 00:27:35.000
And Michael has a line when he's meeting Holly for the first time.
迈克尔在第一次见到霍莉时说过一句台词。

611
00:27:35.480 --> 00:27:42.160
And he says that his job is to, quote, make the office fun, while HR's job is to make the office lame.
他说他的工作是，引用一下，让办公室变得有趣，而人力资源部的工作是让办公室变得无聊。

612
00:27:42.700 --> 00:27:44.600
So Toby's the fun stopper.
所以托比就是那个扫兴的人。

613
00:27:44.600 --> 00:27:45.240
Yes.
没错。

614
00:27:45.480 --> 00:27:46.640
And we kind of knew that.
我们其实也知道这一点。

615
00:27:46.920 --> 00:27:52.140
But then I found this amazing interview with Paul Lieberstein, where he talks about this.
但我后来找到了保罗·李伯斯坦的一个精彩采访，他在里面谈到了这件事。

616
00:27:52.500 --> 00:27:58.500
How did they come up with, in the writer's room, this dynamic of Michael hating Toby so much?
编剧室当初是怎么想出迈克尔如此讨厌托比这种设定的呢？

617
00:27:58.680 --> 00:28:04.440
And he said that Michael's hatred of Toby goes back to a deleted scene from the Alliance.
他说迈克尔对托比的仇恨可以追溯到《联盟》那一集里的一段删减片段。

618
00:28:04.920 --> 00:28:08.780
This is where they found this, like, true hatred of Toby.
他们就是在那里发现了这种对托比真正的仇恨。

619
00:28:09.340 --> 00:28:13.920
In the scene, Toby is coming in to sign Meredith's birthday card.
在那个场景里，托比进来给梅雷迪思的生日贺卡签名。

620
00:28:14.600 --> 00:28:18.720
And Paul said, I just go in, write something quickly, and leave.
保罗说，我当时就是走进去，随便写点什么，然后离开。

621
00:28:18.840 --> 00:28:19.700
That's the scene.
就是那个场景。

622
00:28:19.840 --> 00:28:27.120
But when they were shooting the scene, I guess it took Paul a long time to physically write down what he was going to write down.
但在拍摄那个场景时，我猜保罗花了好长时间才写完他要写的东西。

623
00:28:27.340 --> 00:28:32.040
I have a memory of this, that he was writing in the card, and it took a bit.
我记得这件事，他当时在卡片上写字，花了一点时间。

624
00:28:32.760 --> 00:28:39.480
Paul said, I could just feel him watching me, and I could feel this hatred burning.
保罗说，我能感觉到他在盯着我看，我能感觉到那种燃烧的仇恨。

625
00:28:39.480 --> 00:28:48.500
And he said that Steve told him afterwards that it was in that moment that he decided, as Michael, to hate Toby.
他说史蒂夫事后告诉他，就是在那一刻，他决定以迈克尔的身份去讨厌托比。

626
00:28:49.820 --> 00:28:55.740
And then Paul said, it's really terrifying to act with Steve because he misses nothing.
保罗还说，和史蒂夫演对手戏真的很可怕，因为他什么细节都不会放过。

627
00:28:56.500 --> 00:29:05.400
And that was when they ran with it, that Paul went to the writers and said, Michael hates Toby.
于是他们就顺着这个思路演下去了，保罗跑去告诉编剧们，迈克尔讨厌托比。

628
00:29:06.580 --> 00:29:11.440
Because you know, if Jim took a long time to write a message, he would have all the patience in the world.
因为你知道，如果吉姆花很长时间写留言，他会有全世界的耐心。

629
00:29:11.660 --> 00:29:11.840
Yeah.
是啊。

630
00:29:11.840 --> 00:29:16.160
But Toby not really knowing what to write and taking a bit.
但托比不知道写什么，还磨磨蹭蹭的。

631
00:29:16.320 --> 00:29:17.140
Michael's like, ah!
迈克尔就觉得，啊！

632
00:29:17.560 --> 00:29:17.800
Yeah.
没错。

633
00:29:18.660 --> 00:29:24.860
And then, of course, that led to one of my favorite lines, I hate so much about the way you choose to be.
当然，这也引出了我最喜欢的台词之一：我非常讨厌你选择成为的那种人。

634
00:29:25.020 --> 00:29:25.320
Yeah.
是啊。

635
00:29:25.500 --> 00:29:28.000
Which is what sums it all up.
这简直总结了一切。

636
00:29:28.100 --> 00:29:28.320
Yeah.
没错。

637
00:29:28.600 --> 00:29:31.380
We're about to start a whole new story arc for Pam.
我们马上要开启帕姆的一个全新故事线了。

638
00:29:32.300 --> 00:29:34.060
She's not having a great sales day.
她今天的销售业绩不太好。

639
00:29:34.480 --> 00:29:35.280
I know.
我知道。

640
00:29:35.420 --> 00:29:37.640
She's just going to own that she sucks at it.
她决定坦然接受自己不擅长销售的事实。

641
00:29:37.640 --> 00:29:39.680
She, like, puts her head on her desk.
她把头埋在桌子上。

642
00:29:39.780 --> 00:29:41.160
And Jim knows, too.
吉姆也看出来了。

643
00:29:41.920 --> 00:29:42.140
Yeah.
是啊。

644
00:29:42.300 --> 00:29:44.600
We had a fan question from Cassandra P.
我们收到了一位来自威斯康星州麦迪逊市的粉丝卡桑德拉·P的提问，

645
00:29:44.760 --> 00:29:47.520
in Madison, Wisconsin, who said,
她说，

646
00:29:47.680 --> 00:29:56.100
this is one of my favorite Office episodes, and if I had an Angela-style note card to describe this episode, I would call it Full Pam.
这是我最喜欢的《办公室》剧集之一，如果我有一张安吉拉风格的卡片来描述这一集，我会称之为“完全的帕姆”。

647
00:29:56.400 --> 00:29:57.720
Oh, I love it!
噢，我太喜欢这个说法了！

648
00:29:58.060 --> 00:30:04.480
Pam truly becomes the main character in this episode, and it sets her up for empowerment and strength for the rest of the series.
帕姆在这一集中真正成为了主角，这为她后续剧集中的赋权和成长奠定了基础。

649
00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:08.540
Also, this season, Pam's makeup is 100% on point.
另外，这一季帕姆的妆容简直完美。

650
00:30:08.800 --> 00:30:09.620
Go, Pam!
加油，帕姆！

651
00:30:09.980 --> 00:30:11.820
Oh, you look super cute.
噢，你看上去超级可爱。

652
00:30:12.280 --> 00:30:13.140
I know!
我知道！

653
00:30:13.380 --> 00:30:15.140
Pam got really good with eyeliner.
帕姆的眼线画得真好。

654
00:30:15.460 --> 00:30:16.000
She did!
确实！

655
00:30:16.080 --> 00:30:17.460
I don't know what happened to her over the summer.
我不知道她那个暑假经历了什么。

656
00:30:17.620 --> 00:30:21.120
Like we said, I got married over the summer, so I was just glowing.
就像我们说的，我那个暑假结婚了，所以整个人都在散发光彩。

657
00:30:21.420 --> 00:30:22.680
I think maybe that's part of it.
我觉得那可能也是原因之一。

658
00:30:22.680 --> 00:30:23.720
You were just a happy person.
你当时就是一个幸福的人。

659
00:30:24.800 --> 00:30:26.040
What's up next, lady?
接下来是什么，女士？

660
00:30:27.100 --> 00:30:27.840
Let's see.
让我看看。

661
00:30:28.140 --> 00:30:32.220
Oh, what's up next is John Krasinski breaking a lot.
噢，接下来是约翰·卡拉辛斯基笑场了。

662
00:30:32.220 --> 00:30:36.040
He is so tickled by Andy coming up to Dwight.
安迪走向德怀特的那一幕让他觉得太好笑了。

663
00:30:36.280 --> 00:30:39.700
It's saying, did you call my clients and use the F word?
台词是，你是不是给我的客户打电话还用了F开头的脏话？

664
00:30:40.220 --> 00:30:40.700
Yeah.
没错。

665
00:30:41.300 --> 00:30:42.200
There it is.
就是那儿。

666
00:30:42.400 --> 00:30:43.880
Five minutes, 13 seconds.
五分十三秒。

667
00:30:44.300 --> 00:30:47.720
John is looking at Ed, and it clearly starts breaking in the background.
约翰看着艾德，背景里他明显开始笑场了。

668
00:30:48.200 --> 00:30:51.760
Well, we find out why Dwight wants to boycott the Steamtown Mall.
嗯，我们发现了德怀特为什么要抵制蒸汽镇购物中心的原因。

669
00:30:52.080 --> 00:30:57.160
It's because he went there with Moe's, and he went to Precious Heirlooms, and they wouldn't let him in.
因为他当时和莫斯一起去那儿，想进“珍贵传家宝”店，结果被拒之门外。

670
00:30:57.160 --> 00:31:01.700
Yeah, he saw this amazing wizard holding a crystal.
对，他看到了一个拿着水晶的超酷巫师。

671
00:31:02.080 --> 00:31:04.640
Yeah, he wanted this nice thing.
是啊，他想要那个好东西。

672
00:31:04.800 --> 00:31:07.740
He so rarely treats himself to nice things.
他很少给自己买什么好东西。

673
00:31:08.000 --> 00:31:08.420
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

674
00:31:08.860 --> 00:31:10.700
He made himself vulnerable.
他难得敞开心扉。

675
00:31:11.060 --> 00:31:11.460
Yeah.
是啊。

676
00:31:11.620 --> 00:31:14.760
He wanted it, and they denied him entry.
他想要那个东西，结果被拒绝入内。

677
00:31:15.360 --> 00:31:18.460
Kelly says, you need a pretty woman there, asses.
凯莉说，你们得带个美女去，混蛋们。

678
00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:19.400
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

679
00:31:19.960 --> 00:31:21.040
Everyone agrees.
大家都同意。

680
00:31:21.460 --> 00:31:24.340
Well, except Creed, who says they should start their own mall.
除了克里德，他说他们应该自己开个购物中心。

681
00:31:24.340 --> 00:31:25.380
Yeah, I know.
是啊，我知道。

682
00:31:26.040 --> 00:31:27.280
I love that line.
我超爱那句台词。

683
00:31:27.960 --> 00:31:31.500
Jim offers to go back to the store with Dwight to teach them a lesson.
吉姆提议和德怀特一起回店里给他们点教训。

684
00:31:31.920 --> 00:31:33.420
Andy's like, I'm coming, too.
安迪说，我也要去。

685
00:31:33.980 --> 00:31:35.960
This starts a hilarious storyline.
这开启了一条搞笑的故事线。

686
00:31:36.920 --> 00:31:44.100
Andy's going to start off with a talking head, where he says, did you assume that I would automatically side with the rich, snobby shop owner?
安迪先是有一个采访镜头，他说，你是不是以为我会自动站在那个有钱、势利的店主那边？

687
00:31:44.260 --> 00:31:48.720
He starts taking off his fancy cufflinks and throwing them, takes off his tie clip.
他开始摘下昂贵的袖扣扔掉，又摘下了领带夹。

688
00:31:49.100 --> 00:31:51.640
There was a candy bag alt for Andy.
安迪当时还有一个关于糖果袋的备选方案。

689
00:31:52.140 --> 00:31:52.940
Oh, please.
噢，拜托。

690
00:31:53.240 --> 00:31:53.560
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

691
00:31:53.560 --> 00:31:54.800
Here's what it said.
它是这么说的。

692
00:31:55.040 --> 00:31:56.360
I love revenge.
我喜欢复仇。

693
00:31:56.640 --> 00:31:58.380
Well, not like violent revenge.
嗯，不是那种暴力的复仇。

694
00:31:58.600 --> 00:31:59.560
Not like Kill Bill.
不是《杀死比尔》那种。

695
00:31:59.860 --> 00:32:01.340
More like Legally Blonde.
更像是《律政俏佳人》那种。

696
00:32:02.040 --> 00:32:04.540
Nobody's getting the top of their skull sliced off today.
今天没人会把头盖骨给削下来。

697
00:32:04.720 --> 00:32:05.640
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

698
00:32:05.820 --> 00:32:06.860
Didn't sign up for that.
我可没签那种合同。

699
00:32:07.140 --> 00:32:07.900
That's right.
没错。

700
00:32:09.940 --> 00:32:12.540
I love that Andy is a Legally Blonde fan.
我喜欢安迪是《律政俏佳人》粉丝这一点。

701
00:32:12.880 --> 00:32:16.840
This leads into my personal favorite talking head.
这引出了我个人最喜欢的采访片段。

702
00:32:16.840 --> 00:32:18.420
It's Dwight.
是德怀特。

703
00:32:18.580 --> 00:32:18.900
It's Dwight.
是德怀特。

704
00:32:18.900 --> 00:32:19.800
And Andy.
还有安迪。

705
00:32:20.040 --> 00:32:20.620
And Jim.
还有吉姆。

706
00:32:20.860 --> 00:32:21.760
And then Kelly.
然后是凯莉。

707
00:32:21.760 --> 00:32:22.340
Yes.
没错。

708
00:32:22.560 --> 00:32:31.380
And all they're trying to do is tell us the famous scene from Pretty Woman, where Julia Roberts gets her revenge on the snooty shop owner.
他们都在试图重现《风月俏佳人》里的经典桥段，就是朱莉娅·罗伯茨向那个势利眼的店主复仇的那一段。

709
00:32:31.620 --> 00:32:31.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

710
00:32:32.060 --> 00:32:32.860
Big mistake.
大错特错。

711
00:32:32.860 --> 00:32:33.100
Big mistake.
大错特错。

712
00:32:33.240 --> 00:32:33.740
Huge.
错得离谱。

713
00:32:34.420 --> 00:32:35.240
That's right.
说得对。

714
00:32:35.740 --> 00:32:39.980
Well, let's take a break, because when we get back, full Pam is happening.
好了，我们休息一下，回来之后，帕姆要大显身手了。

715
00:32:40.580 --> 00:32:41.460
Sure is.
确实如此。

716
00:32:41.560 --> 00:32:43.140
She gets a real big idea.
她想到了一个绝妙的主意。

717
00:32:52.110 --> 00:33:00.450
We're back, and a man enters the office looking for the office administrator, and Pam really perks up.
我们回来了，有个男人走进办公室找行政主管，帕姆立刻精神起来了。

718
00:33:00.630 --> 00:33:01.270
Yes.
没错。

719
00:33:01.710 --> 00:33:03.910
Yes, Pam is like, that's me.
是的，帕姆心想，那是我。

720
00:33:04.450 --> 00:33:06.450
I'm the office administrator.
我是行政主管。

721
00:33:06.450 --> 00:33:08.350
And we are not interested.
但我们不感兴趣。

722
00:33:08.750 --> 00:33:12.730
We don't want your blinds, your window treatments.
我们不需要你的百叶窗，也不需要你的窗帘装饰。

723
00:33:13.150 --> 00:33:16.290
At 8 minutes 40 seconds, I'm busted.
在8分40秒的时候，我被抓包了。

724
00:33:16.730 --> 00:33:17.490
Who's busted?
谁被抓包了？

725
00:33:17.710 --> 00:33:18.430
I'm busted.
我被抓包了。

726
00:33:18.490 --> 00:33:19.570
What are you busted for?
你因为什么被抓包？

727
00:33:19.710 --> 00:33:20.710
I'm playing solitaire.
我在玩纸牌游戏。

728
00:33:20.710 --> 00:33:22.030
On your computer?
在电脑上？

729
00:33:22.250 --> 00:33:23.850
Yes, Angela Martin would never.
是的，安吉拉·马丁绝不会这么做。

730
00:33:24.550 --> 00:33:26.330
Wow, that's very out of character.
哇，这太不像你的风格了。

731
00:33:26.570 --> 00:33:28.830
You should definitely have a spreadsheet on your computer.
你的电脑上确实应该开着电子表格。

732
00:33:29.010 --> 00:33:29.370
I know.
我知道。

733
00:33:30.030 --> 00:33:34.050
Well, I want you to know that we have a guest star in the house.
对了，我想告诉大家，我们今天有位客串明星在场。

734
00:33:34.310 --> 00:33:35.250
Let's hear it.
让我们欢迎他。

735
00:33:35.410 --> 00:33:45.010
Vincent Angelo, who plays the salesperson, has been on Desperate Housewives, Grey's Anatomy, Parks and Recreation, and House.
文森特·安杰洛，饰演推销员的那位，他曾出演过《绝望主妇》、《实习医生格蕾》、《公园与游憩》和《豪斯医生》。

736
00:33:45.870 --> 00:33:46.890
It's my new favorite.
这是我的新宠。

737
00:33:47.090 --> 00:33:50.330
I don't know what I like more, discovering someone has been on Monk or House.
我不知道发现某人演过《神探阿蒙》还是《豪斯医生》更让我开心。

738
00:33:50.330 --> 00:33:52.750
You just like seeing a guest star in the house.
你就是喜欢看到有客串明星在场。

739
00:33:52.750 --> 00:33:53.150
I know.
我知道。

740
00:33:53.270 --> 00:33:54.450
When they've been on House.
尤其是当他们演过《豪斯医生》的时候。

741
00:33:54.610 --> 00:33:55.310
It's become my favorite.
这已经成了我的最爱。

742
00:33:55.590 --> 00:34:01.230
I also like tracking if people have played more than one character on Law & Order.
我还喜欢追踪演员是否在《法律与秩序》里演过不止一个角色。

743
00:34:01.710 --> 00:34:05.330
I love the big pause you took before Law & Order.
我喜欢你在说《法律与秩序》之前停顿的那一下。

744
00:34:05.530 --> 00:34:05.890
I know.
我知道。

745
00:34:06.010 --> 00:34:06.990
That's the summer cold.
那是夏季感冒闹的。

746
00:34:07.150 --> 00:34:07.590
That is.
确实是。

747
00:34:07.750 --> 00:34:08.590
Summer cold.
夏季感冒。

748
00:34:08.590 --> 00:34:11.030
It has you just one second delayed.
它让你慢了整整一秒。

749
00:34:11.510 --> 00:34:13.330
It's like you're on a satellite feed.
就像你在用卫星信号通话一样。

750
00:34:14.230 --> 00:34:19.890
Well, Pam's going to have a talking head now where she says, there's a few ways you can get promoted.
好了，现在是帕姆的采访片段，她说，晋升有几种途径。

751
00:34:20.910 --> 00:34:23.670
One, you can wait for an opening, a new job.
第一种，你可以等一个空缺，一份新工作。

752
00:34:23.670 --> 00:34:24.810
You apply for it.
然后去申请。

753
00:34:25.090 --> 00:34:26.270
That's the main way.
这是主要途径。

754
00:34:26.390 --> 00:34:26.750
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

755
00:34:26.970 --> 00:34:31.810
Or this way, where you just apparently lie yourself into a new job.
或者像这样，显然是靠撒谎给自己弄了个新职位。

756
00:34:32.150 --> 00:34:33.910
So Pam is going to go into the kitchen.
所以帕姆走进厨房。

757
00:34:34.050 --> 00:34:35.990
She's going to make herself a cup of tea.
她给自己泡了杯茶。

758
00:34:37.030 --> 00:34:40.570
Oscar's like, what's up with your new position?
奥斯卡问，你的新职位是怎么回事？

759
00:34:40.810 --> 00:34:41.250
Congratulations.
恭喜啊。

760
00:34:41.870 --> 00:34:47.570
And she's clearly trying to suss out from Oscar, what is a reasonable salary for this position?
她显然是想从奥斯卡那儿套出这个职位合理的薪水是多少。

761
00:34:47.810 --> 00:34:50.310
So she's like, yeah, I'm going to make 40K, maybe 50.
所以她说，嗯，我大概能拿4万，或者5万吧。

762
00:34:50.350 --> 00:34:51.190
He's like, 50?
他说，5万？

763
00:34:51.510 --> 00:34:54.410
She's like, no, no, it's like 41 and a half.
她说，不不，大概是4万1千5。

764
00:34:54.690 --> 00:34:56.230
Yeah, 41.5.
对，4万1千5。

765
00:34:57.210 --> 00:35:01.710
Lady, we got some mail about this storyline, and both of these delighted me.
女士，我们收到了一些关于这个剧情的来信，这两封都让我很开心。

766
00:35:01.890 --> 00:35:02.350
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

767
00:35:02.530 --> 00:35:03.710
I feel so proud.
我感到非常自豪。

768
00:35:04.090 --> 00:35:06.170
The first one is from Kelly M.
第一封来自澳大利亚墨尔本的凯莉·M。

769
00:35:06.310 --> 00:35:08.230
in Melbourne, Australia, who said,
她说，

770
00:35:08.230 --> 00:35:12.690
a couple of years ago, I was inspired by Pam's storyline in this episode
几年前，我受到了这一集中帕姆剧情的启发，

771
00:35:12.690 --> 00:35:15.990
where she just starts telling people she's the office administrator.
就是她开始告诉别人她是办公室行政主管的那段。

772
00:35:16.310 --> 00:35:17.890
So I did it myself.
于是我也照做了。

773
00:35:18.230 --> 00:35:18.690
What?
什么？

