好的。

1101
00:48:37.380 --> 00:48:44.180
And Pam explains that this office has a lot of one-person departments.
帕姆解释说，这个办公室里有很多“一人部门”。

1102
00:48:44.560 --> 00:48:46.680
So there are a lot of department heads.
所以有很多部门主管。

1103
00:48:46.840 --> 00:48:48.260
Which I didn't realize.
这一点我之前没意识到。

1104
00:48:48.260 --> 00:48:50.960
I didn't realize Meredith was the head of a department.
我没意识到梅雷迪思竟然也是个部门主管。

1105
00:48:51.300 --> 00:48:51.660
Yeah.
是啊。

1106
00:48:51.900 --> 00:48:55.320
Isn't she the head of, like, quality control or something?
她不是负责质量控制之类的吗？

1107
00:48:55.560 --> 00:48:56.680
Isn't it just her and Creed?
难道不是只有她和克里德两个人吗？

1108
00:48:57.140 --> 00:48:58.140
I don't know.
我不知道。

1109
00:48:58.780 --> 00:48:59.960
I wasn't sure.
我不确定。

1110
00:49:00.100 --> 00:49:02.140
But first she goes in and gets Michael's signature.
但首先她走进去拿到了迈克尔的签名。

1111
00:49:02.140 --> 00:49:04.460
He is still upset about his counseling.
他还在为自己的心理咨询感到心烦。

1112
00:49:04.460 --> 00:49:05.580
He doesn't look at the form.
他看都没看那张表格。

1113
00:49:05.580 --> 00:49:07.440
He doesn't ask her any questions.
他什么问题也没问她。

1114
00:49:08.440 --> 00:49:11.780
Then she's going to go over to Meredith.
然后她要去梅雷迪思那边。

1115
00:49:11.780 --> 00:49:14.260
What are you doing in this scene?
这一幕里你在做什么？

1116
00:49:14.400 --> 00:49:16.840
It looks like you're, I don't know what you're doing.
看起来你是在……我不知道你在做什么。

1117
00:49:17.000 --> 00:49:17.740
A dance move.
一个舞蹈动作。

1118
00:49:17.900 --> 00:49:20.120
You're kind of, what is this?
你有点……这是什么？

1119
00:49:20.460 --> 00:49:20.780
Yes.
是的。

1120
00:49:20.840 --> 00:49:22.320
We got questions about this.
我们收到了关于这一幕的问题。

1121
00:49:23.140 --> 00:49:23.620
Abby S.
来自佐治亚州亚特兰大的艾比·S。

1122
00:49:23.700 --> 00:49:28.580
from Atlanta, Georgia would also like to know, what the hell is Pam saying or doing with Meredith?
她也想知道，帕姆对梅雷迪思到底在说什么或做什么？

1123
00:49:28.580 --> 00:49:30.200
Larissa W.
来自科罗拉多州利特尔顿的拉丽莎·W。

1124
00:49:30.540 --> 00:49:36.280
from Littleton, Colorado says, did I have scripted lines or was I improvising?
她说，我是照着剧本演的，还是即兴发挥的？

1125
00:49:36.480 --> 00:49:38.560
Because it's, you know, voiceover.
因为那是旁白。

1126
00:49:38.800 --> 00:49:39.040
Yeah.
没错。

1127
00:49:39.160 --> 00:49:39.920
With a talking head.
配合着采访镜头。

1128
00:49:40.460 --> 00:49:42.140
Here's what it said in the script.
剧本上是这么写的。

1129
00:49:42.960 --> 00:49:43.800
B-roll.
空镜素材。

1130
00:49:44.660 --> 00:49:48.300
Pam makes ribald humping gesture by Meredith's desk.
帕姆在梅雷迪思的办公桌旁做了一个粗俗的耸动动作。

1131
00:49:48.300 --> 00:49:53.800
I thought it was a humping gesture, but I didn't want to throw that out there in case this was some dance move.
我以为那是耸动动作，但我不敢直接说出来，万一那是个舞蹈动作呢。

1132
00:49:53.900 --> 00:49:54.420
I didn't know.
我当时不知道。

1133
00:49:54.640 --> 00:50:00.500
Well, first of all, when I read the stage direction, I had to look up the definition of ribald.
好吧，首先，当我读到舞台提示时，我不得不去查“ribald”（粗俗的）这个词的定义。

1134
00:50:01.200 --> 00:50:07.300
And it means referring to a sexual matter in an amusingly coarse or irreverent way.
它的意思是：以一种有趣但粗鲁或不敬的方式谈论性事。

1135
00:50:07.580 --> 00:50:09.280
A synonym is body.
同义词是“下流”。

1136
00:50:09.860 --> 00:50:17.720
And I'll have you know, standards and practices, when they read the script, they had something to say about this gesture.
而且我要告诉你，审查部门在读到剧本时，对这个动作有话要说。

1137
00:50:17.720 --> 00:50:19.180
Please tell me what they said.
快告诉我他们说了什么。

1138
00:50:19.380 --> 00:50:27.200
They said, quote, please use your discretion staging the scene where Pam makes a, quote, ribald humping gesture.
他们说，引用：“请在安排帕姆做那个‘粗俗耸动动作’的场景时，自行斟酌。”

1139
00:50:27.600 --> 00:50:30.640
It should play as funny, not explicit.
“表演效果应该是搞笑的，而不是露骨的。”

1140
00:50:31.440 --> 00:50:33.180
Man, Pam is working it.
天哪，帕姆真是太卖力了。

1141
00:50:33.300 --> 00:50:35.440
She knows what's going to work with each person.
她知道对每个人该用什么招数。

1142
00:50:35.640 --> 00:50:36.400
She really does.
她确实知道。

1143
00:50:36.580 --> 00:50:45.840
It says at Angela's desk, Pam points to various cat pictures and rearranges them more nicely on her desk, lighting Angela up, who signs as she talks.
剧本上写着：在安吉拉的办公桌前，帕姆指着各种猫的照片，把它们重新摆放得更整齐，这让安吉拉很高兴，她在说话时签了字。

1144
00:50:46.620 --> 00:50:48.520
Then Pam is going to go into Daryl's office,
然后帕姆要走进达里尔的办公室，

1145
00:50:48.520 --> 00:50:59.040
and he's very interested in her new position because he might like to have corkboard all over his office because it's something that he saw that Kate Walsh has done to her home office.
他对她的新职位非常感兴趣，因为他也想在办公室里贴满软木板，这是他看到凯特·沃尔什在她的家庭办公室里做过的事。

1146
00:50:59.040 --> 00:51:00.100
He saw it on TV.
他在电视上看到的。

1147
00:51:01.100 --> 00:51:02.660
This got me so tickled.
这让我觉得太好笑了。

1148
00:51:03.020 --> 00:51:05.520
You guys know Kate Walsh is one of my good, good pals.
你们知道凯特·沃尔什是我非常非常好的朋友。

1149
00:51:05.760 --> 00:51:07.760
We go way back to our improv days.
我们从即兴表演时期就认识了。

1150
00:51:07.920 --> 00:51:10.180
Jenna, you know, you even did improv with us one time.
珍娜，你知道，你甚至有一次还和我们一起做过即兴表演。

1151
00:51:10.520 --> 00:51:11.720
Oh, yeah, that's right.
哦，对，没错。

1152
00:51:11.820 --> 00:51:12.040
Yeah.
是啊。

1153
00:51:12.040 --> 00:51:12.740
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1154
00:51:12.800 --> 00:51:14.760
We drug you into one of our improv shows.
我们把你拉进了一场我们的即兴表演里。

1155
00:51:14.940 --> 00:51:20.340
But you guys might also know her as Addison from Grey's Anatomy, plus a gazillion other things she's done.
但你们可能也知道她是《实习医生格蕾》里的艾迪森，此外她还演过数不清的其他作品。

1156
00:51:21.000 --> 00:51:24.860
So when I saw Daryl mention her, I was like, oh, my God.
所以当我看到达里尔提到她时，我就想，天哪。

1157
00:51:25.100 --> 00:51:31.060
So I called Kate, and I said, Kate, did you know you're mentioned in this office episode by Daryl?
于是我给凯特打了电话，我说，凯特，你知道你在那集《办公室》里被达里尔提到了吗？

1158
00:51:31.200 --> 00:51:33.160
And she was like, no, I had no idea.
她说，不知道，我完全没头绪。

1159
00:51:33.380 --> 00:51:38.280
And I said, yeah, I mean, Daryl in the episode says he saw your home office, and it's covered in corkboard.
我说，是啊，我是说，达里尔在那集里说他看到了你的家庭办公室，上面贴满了软木板。

1160
00:51:38.280 --> 00:51:40.160
What do you have to say about that?
你对此有什么想说的吗？

1161
00:51:40.400 --> 00:51:41.740
And here's what she had to say.
以下是她的回应。

1162
00:51:42.680 --> 00:51:44.240
Hi, this is Kate Walsh.
嗨，我是凯特·沃尔什。

1163
00:51:44.380 --> 00:51:50.760
I have never had a home office covered in corkboard, but now I'm wondering why I haven't.
我的家庭办公室从来没贴过软木板，但现在我在想为什么我没这么做。

1164
00:51:50.860 --> 00:51:51.940
That sounds delightful.
听起来真不错。

1165
00:51:55.820 --> 00:51:57.460
I do love a pin board.
我确实很喜欢软木板。

1166
00:52:02.270 --> 00:52:03.710
I love her so much.
我太喜欢她了。

1167
00:52:03.990 --> 00:52:04.770
Thanks, Kate.
谢谢你，凯特。

1168
00:52:05.870 --> 00:52:07.850
Well, I spotted something in Daryl's office.
嗯，我在达里尔的办公室里发现了一些东西。

1169
00:52:07.850 --> 00:52:16.390
It's not corkboard, but at 16 minutes and 53 seconds, there's a blue football helmet with a white paw print hanging on his, like, coat rack thing.
不是软木板，但在16分53秒的时候，他的衣帽架上挂着一个蓝色的橄榄球头盔，上面有个白色的爪印。

1170
00:52:16.410 --> 00:52:17.310
Yeah, I saw it, too.
是啊，我也看到了。

1171
00:52:17.530 --> 00:52:20.590
It's the Valley View High School Cougars football helmet.
那是山谷景观高中的美洲狮队橄榄球头盔。

1172
00:52:20.790 --> 00:52:22.770
And I just thought that was an amazing detail.
我觉得那是个很棒的细节。

1173
00:52:22.890 --> 00:52:26.630
And that's where Pam went to high school, and I guess Daryl did, too, and played football?
那是帕姆读的高中，我猜达里尔也是那里的，还打过橄榄球？

1174
00:52:26.850 --> 00:52:28.050
With Roy, probably.
可能和罗伊一起打的。

1175
00:52:28.210 --> 00:52:28.870
Maybe so.
也许吧。

1176
00:52:29.490 --> 00:52:31.150
Well, full Pam might be in trouble.
好吧，帕姆可能要有麻烦了。

1177
00:52:31.890 --> 00:52:32.390
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1178
00:52:32.390 --> 00:52:39.430
Because Gabe said he's gone through three years' worth of information and can't find anything about Pam being the office administrator.
因为盖博说他查了三年的资料，却找不到任何关于帕姆担任办公室行政主管的记录。

1179
00:52:39.830 --> 00:52:40.170
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1180
00:52:40.370 --> 00:52:45.770
He says he doesn't want to accuse her of anything, so maybe she could just admit.
他说他不想指控她什么，所以也许她能主动承认。

1181
00:52:46.610 --> 00:52:47.870
Pam's like, admit what?
帕姆心想，承认什么？

1182
00:52:48.770 --> 00:52:57.030
Pam realizes that Gabe is so afraid of confrontation that he will not accuse her of being a liar or making it up.
帕姆意识到盖博非常害怕冲突，以至于他不会指控她撒谎或编造事实。

1183
00:52:57.190 --> 00:52:58.310
He won't do it.
他做不到。

1184
00:52:58.390 --> 00:52:59.650
He won't do it.
他不会做的。

1185
00:52:59.650 --> 00:53:06.470
And then he folds, and Pam says, let me know if you need a new chair or anything that an office administrator can handle.
然后他妥协了，帕姆说，如果你需要新椅子或者任何办公室行政主管能处理的事，随时告诉我。

1186
00:53:06.690 --> 00:53:10.270
And Gabe says, can I get one of those nameplates that says Gabe Lewis?
盖博说，我能要一个写着“盖博·刘易斯”的姓名牌吗？

1187
00:53:10.530 --> 00:53:11.490
Pam says, sure.
帕姆说，当然可以。

1188
00:53:11.690 --> 00:53:12.410
Anything else?
还有别的吗？

1189
00:53:12.490 --> 00:53:13.130
He says, nope.
他说，没了。

1190
00:53:13.330 --> 00:53:14.330
And that's it.
事情就这样成了。

1191
00:53:14.610 --> 00:53:16.350
She's the office administrator.
她成了办公室行政主管。

1192
00:53:16.690 --> 00:53:17.010
It's done.
搞定。

1193
00:53:17.790 --> 00:53:25.290
Pam has a talking head where she says, the first lesson of watching World Poker Tour at 2 a.m., you play the opponent, not the cards.
帕姆有个访谈镜头，她说，凌晨两点看世界扑克巡回赛学到的第一课就是，你要对付的是对手，而不是牌。

1194
00:53:25.290 --> 00:53:27.870
Lady, we got a fan question from Natalie F.
女士们，我们收到一个来自德克萨斯州圣安东尼奥市娜塔莉·F的粉丝提问。

1195
00:53:27.950 --> 00:53:33.890
in San Antonio, Texas, who would like to know, what do you guys think about the way Pam gets her promotion?
她想知道，你们觉得帕姆获得晋升的方式怎么样？

1196
00:53:34.170 --> 00:53:40.230
The first time I watched it, I was excited for her, but in re-watching it, I was kind of bothered by her dishonesty.
我第一次看的时候，为她感到兴奋，但重看的时候，我被她的不诚实困扰了。

1197
00:53:41.110 --> 00:53:42.050
What do we think?
我们怎么看？

1198
00:53:42.450 --> 00:53:45.150
I mean, Natalie, it's a little layered, right?
我是说，娜塔莉，这有点复杂，对吧？

1199
00:53:45.150 --> 00:53:51.370
Because I'm so happy Pam finally was an advocate for herself and made something happen.
因为我很高兴帕姆终于能为自己争取，并促成了这件事。

1200
00:53:52.010 --> 00:53:56.730
Natalie, I lied all the time when I was an up-and-coming actress.
娜塔莉，我刚出道当演员的时候也经常撒谎。

1201
00:53:57.430 --> 00:54:01.010
If I had an audition, I lied and said I had a dental appointment.
如果我有试镜，我会撒谎说我有牙医预约。

1202
00:54:01.570 --> 00:54:02.530
It was just easier.
这样比较省事。

1203
00:54:02.530 --> 00:54:03.350
To get out of work.
为了逃避工作。

1204
00:54:03.530 --> 00:54:03.790
Yeah.
没错。

1205
00:54:04.030 --> 00:54:06.570
Well, you guys know how I got my internship on Conan O'Brien.
好吧，你们知道我是怎么得到柯南·奥布莱恩节目实习机会的吧。

1206
00:54:06.630 --> 00:54:07.750
That's what I was going to say.
我正想说这个。

1207
00:54:07.750 --> 00:54:08.690
You shared that.
你分享过那件事。

1208
00:54:08.910 --> 00:54:11.310
You totally just lied your way into it.
你完全就是靠撒谎混进去的。

1209
00:54:11.310 --> 00:54:13.470
I just kept calling and saying, yeah, I just spoke to someone.
我就是一直打电话说，对，我刚和某人谈过了。

1210
00:54:13.590 --> 00:54:14.330
They said I'm hired.
他们说我被录用了。

1211
00:54:15.150 --> 00:54:15.350
I know.
我知道。

1212
00:54:15.470 --> 00:54:20.750
I guess it begs the question, like, when is it unethical and when is it ambition?
我想这引出了一个问题，就是什么时候是不道德的，什么时候是雄心壮志？

1213
00:54:21.810 --> 00:54:24.770
When is it to be admired and when is it to be faulted?
什么时候该被赞赏，什么时候该被指责？

1214
00:54:25.050 --> 00:54:25.450
Yeah.
是啊。

1215
00:54:25.490 --> 00:54:26.950
I think it's layered, Natalie.
我觉得这很复杂，娜塔莉。

1216
00:54:27.370 --> 00:54:28.910
I'm happy for her in this moment.
我为她此刻感到高兴。

1217
00:54:29.130 --> 00:54:33.970
I bet Mike Schur's book, How to Be Perfect, would tell us the moral answer to this question.
我敢说迈克·舒尔的书《如何变得完美》会告诉我们这个问题的道德答案。

1218
00:54:34.030 --> 00:54:34.330
Yes.
没错。

1219
00:54:34.570 --> 00:54:35.830
Perhaps we should ask him.
也许我们该问问他。

1220
00:54:35.890 --> 00:54:39.290
Did Pam getting this position benefit everyone else in the office?
帕姆得到这个职位对办公室里的其他人有好处吗？

1221
00:54:39.450 --> 00:54:40.530
Were their lives made better?
他们的生活变得更好了吗？

1222
00:54:41.350 --> 00:54:44.190
So is lying okay if you make other people's lives better?
所以如果你的谎言让别人的生活变得更好，那就可以接受吗？

1223
00:54:44.190 --> 00:54:45.830
See, that's complicated.
你看，这很复杂。

1224
00:54:46.130 --> 00:54:47.190
It's very complicated.
非常复杂。

1225
00:54:47.470 --> 00:54:53.650
And also, you know, people were really liking this moment at first of Pam, but as we get
而且，你知道，起初人们真的很喜欢帕姆的这个时刻，但随着我们深入了解

1226
00:54:53.650 --> 00:54:58.630
into some of the things she's going to do as office administrator, people turned on her.
她作为办公室行政主管要做的一些事情，人们开始反感她了。

1227
00:54:58.790 --> 00:54:59.070
Yeah.
确实。

1228
00:54:59.230 --> 00:55:00.230
We'll discuss it.
我们会讨论这个的。

1229
00:55:00.350 --> 00:55:04.730
And when I say people, I mean fans turned on the storyline because Pam starts kind of using
当我提到人们时，我是指粉丝们开始反感这个剧情，因为帕姆开始以某种方式利用

1230
00:55:04.730 --> 00:55:06.350
her power in ways that maybe...
她的权力，可能……

1231
00:55:06.930 --> 00:55:07.910
Are not appropriate.
不太合适。

1232
00:55:07.910 --> 00:55:09.230
...people didn't care for it.
……人们并不喜欢那样。

1233
00:55:09.230 --> 00:55:10.850
Natalie, great question.
娜塔莉，问得好。

1234
00:55:11.470 --> 00:55:18.510
Lady, let's go to the mall because Jim and Andy have brought Dwight to Precious Heirlooms
女士们，我们去商场吧，因为吉姆和安迪把德怀特带到了“珍贵传家宝”店

1235
00:55:18.510 --> 00:55:20.810
to confront the salesperson.
去和销售员对质。

1236
00:55:20.950 --> 00:55:22.130
To get his revenge.
去报仇。

1237
00:55:22.870 --> 00:55:25.770
But the salesperson recognizes Dwight.
但销售员认出了德怀特。

1238
00:55:25.910 --> 00:55:27.170
He's like, oh, I remember you.
他说，哦，我记得你。

1239
00:55:27.290 --> 00:55:28.890
Yes, you were here yesterday.
是的，你昨天来过这里。

1240
00:55:29.250 --> 00:55:30.070
We took a picture.
我们还拍了张照片。

1241
00:55:30.310 --> 00:55:30.950
We were worried.
我们当时很担心。

1242
00:55:31.110 --> 00:55:34.770
You had bloodstains on your hands and you were wearing overalls.
你手上沾着血迹，还穿着工作服。

1243
00:55:35.150 --> 00:55:37.030
And Jim is like, what?
吉姆当时就懵了，什么？

1244
00:55:37.370 --> 00:55:37.430
Huh?
啊？

1245
00:55:37.430 --> 00:55:37.550
What?
什么？

1246
00:55:37.870 --> 00:55:37.920
What?
什么？

1247
00:55:39.310 --> 00:55:44.010
And yes, there we see why they denied Dwight entry.
是的，我们终于明白他们为什么拒绝德怀特进入了。

1248
00:55:44.370 --> 00:55:46.610
He has his hands.
他手上全是血。

1249
00:55:46.670 --> 00:55:47.810
They're all red.
全红了。

1250
00:55:47.810 --> 00:55:51.150
They're on the glass of Precious HeirlooMs.
都印在“珍贵传家宝”的玻璃上了。

1251
00:55:51.290 --> 00:55:56.030
But Dwight is still going to try to have his pretty woman moment.
但德怀特还是想尝试一下他的《风月俏佳人》时刻。

1252
00:55:56.350 --> 00:55:57.170
He is.
确实。

1253
00:55:57.370 --> 00:56:00.050
He still wants to go pretty woman on their ass.
他还是想对他们来一场《风月俏佳人》式的报复。

1254
00:56:00.190 --> 00:56:01.830
And I have the question for you.
我有个问题要问你。

1255
00:56:02.010 --> 00:56:04.310
I'm titling this, Who Did It Best?
我给这部分起名叫“谁演得最好？”

1256
00:56:04.790 --> 00:56:05.390
Julia?
朱莉娅？

1257
00:56:06.370 --> 00:56:06.970
Hi.
嗨。

1258
00:56:07.250 --> 00:56:07.530
Hello.
你好。

1259
00:56:07.790 --> 00:56:08.590
Do you remember me?
你还记得我吗？

1260
00:56:08.870 --> 00:56:10.010
No, I'm sorry.
不，抱歉。

1261
00:56:10.010 --> 00:56:11.270
I was in here yesterday.
我昨天来过这里。

1262
00:56:11.270 --> 00:56:12.270
You wouldn't wait on me?
你当时不肯接待我？

1263
00:56:12.510 --> 00:56:13.110
Oh.
哦。

1264
00:56:13.450 --> 00:56:14.710
You work on commission, right?
你们是拿提成的，对吧？

1265
00:56:15.390 --> 00:56:15.910
Yes.
是的。

1266
00:56:15.910 --> 00:56:16.110
Yes.
是的。

1267
00:56:17.110 --> 00:56:18.130
Big mistake.
大错特错。

1268
00:56:18.530 --> 00:56:18.990
Big.
很大。

1269
00:56:19.210 --> 00:56:19.630
Huge.
非常大。

1270
00:56:19.970 --> 00:56:21.610
I have to go shopping now.
我现在得去购物了。

1271
00:56:24.230 --> 00:56:25.250
Or Dwight.
或者德怀特。

1272
00:56:25.470 --> 00:56:28.130
When I came to your fineSt...
当我来到你们这家高级……

1273
00:56:28.130 --> 00:56:28.750
You are...
你真是……

1274
00:56:28.750 --> 00:56:29.490
I'm gonna...
我打算……

1275
00:56:29.490 --> 00:56:29.850
Okay.
好吧。

1276
00:56:30.830 --> 00:56:31.390
Listen.
听着。

1277
00:56:31.670 --> 00:56:32.890
You can't treat me.
你不能这样对待我。

1278
00:56:33.290 --> 00:56:33.690
Thank you.
谢谢。

1279
00:56:33.830 --> 00:56:34.590
Good morning, sir.
早上好，先生。

1280
00:56:34.910 --> 00:56:35.390
Okay.
好的。

1281
00:56:35.710 --> 00:56:36.130
Let's go.
我们走吧。

1282
00:56:36.410 --> 00:56:37.930
You made a big mistake.
你犯了个大错。

1283
00:56:38.170 --> 00:56:38.670
Huge.
非常大。

1284
00:56:40.190 --> 00:56:40.990
There it is.
就是这样。

1285
00:56:41.350 --> 00:56:43.590
I mean, Dwight just keeps...
我是说，德怀特一直在……

1286
00:56:43.590 --> 00:56:45.630
He's like this robot that's malfunctioning.
他就像个出了故障的机器人。

1287
00:56:45.730 --> 00:56:46.930
He's like, good morning, good day, sir.
他一会儿说早上好，一会儿说祝您今天愉快，先生。

1288
00:56:46.930 --> 00:56:47.410
Hello.
你好。

1289
00:56:47.730 --> 00:56:48.290
Top of the morning.
早上好。

1290
00:56:48.450 --> 00:56:48.630
What?
什么？

1291
00:56:48.790 --> 00:56:49.490
How dare you?
你怎么敢这样？

1292
00:56:49.770 --> 00:56:50.430
He's like...
他就像是……

1293
00:56:50.870 --> 00:56:53.910
Well, lady, I have got another guest star alert.
好了，女士们，我又要发布客串明星预警了。

1294
00:56:54.290 --> 00:56:57.790
Eric Zuckerman played the salesperson.
埃里克·祖克曼饰演了那个销售员。

1295
00:56:57.790 --> 00:57:02.470
And I've got an interesting bit of trivia on Eric because he falls into my other favorite
关于埃里克，我有一个有趣的冷知识，因为他属于我提到的另一个我最喜欢的

1296
00:57:02.470 --> 00:57:03.830
category that I mentioned.
类别。

1297
00:57:04.470 --> 00:57:10.290
He has not only played two different characters in two different episodes of Law & Order.
他不仅在《法律与秩序》的两集里饰演过两个不同的角色。

1298
00:57:10.490 --> 00:57:13.650
He's also done it on Law & Order Criminal Intent.
他还曾在《法律与秩序：犯罪倾向》中这样做过。

1299
00:57:14.190 --> 00:57:16.510
Multiple characters across the franchise.
在整个系列中饰演过多个角色。

1300
00:57:16.930 --> 00:57:17.270
Yes.
是的。

1301
00:57:17.590 --> 00:57:21.490
He's also had recurring roles on Revenge and Orange is the New Black.
他还曾在《复仇》和《女子监狱》中担任常驻角色。

1302
00:57:21.750 --> 00:57:24.110
I also have a bag breakdown.
我还有一个关于包的细节拆解。

1303
00:57:24.690 --> 00:57:25.710
Dwight's bags?
德怀特的包？

1304
00:57:25.990 --> 00:57:26.330
Yeah.
对。

1305
00:57:26.490 --> 00:57:27.490
All of his shopping bags?
他所有的购物袋吗？

1306
00:57:27.490 --> 00:57:27.950
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1307
00:57:28.130 --> 00:57:32.750
One of them is a Steamtown Mall bag, and the other is from a store called La Tida.
其中一个是蒸汽镇购物中心的袋子，另一个来自一家叫La Tida的店。

1308
00:57:33.170 --> 00:57:35.110
Have we featured La Tida before?
我们之前介绍过La Tida吗？

1309
00:57:35.510 --> 00:57:38.810
I'm not sure, but they're a real store in the Steamtown Mall.
我不确定，但它们确实是蒸汽镇购物中心里的一家真实商店。

1310
00:57:39.030 --> 00:57:43.210
They were there from the day it opened until it closed in 2019.
从商场开业那天起，一直到2019年关门，他们都在那里。

1311
00:57:43.210 --> 00:57:45.830
What did La Tida sell?
La Tida卖什么？

1312
00:57:46.050 --> 00:57:51.970
They sold, like, fancy trinkets and nice items for your house, for giving gifts.
他们卖一些精致的小饰品和家居好物，适合送礼的那种。

1313
00:57:52.430 --> 00:57:54.610
Dwight is on a fancy shopping spree.
德怀特这是在疯狂购物啊。

1314
00:57:54.790 --> 00:57:56.070
He certainly is.
确实是。

1315
00:57:56.070 --> 00:57:59.930
If he's shopping at La Tida, that should tell Precious Heirlooms something.
如果他在La Tida购物，那应该能给“珍贵传家宝”店提个醒。

1316
00:58:00.230 --> 00:58:00.610
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1317
00:58:01.610 --> 00:58:04.450
Before he leaves, he's going to go ahead and buy the wizard.
在他离开之前，他打算把那个巫师雕像买下来。

1318
00:58:04.930 --> 00:58:05.530
Yeah.
对。

1319
00:58:05.810 --> 00:58:06.750
And Jim is like, Dwight!
然后吉姆就喊，德怀特！

1320
00:58:07.030 --> 00:58:07.590
I know.
我知道。

1321
00:58:08.150 --> 00:58:09.330
But he buys the wizard.
但他还是买了那个巫师。

1322
00:58:09.650 --> 00:58:11.570
This scene would have continued, Jenna.
这场戏本来是有后续的，珍娜。

1323
00:58:11.930 --> 00:58:18.410
They would have left the store, and as they're leaving, Dwight smashes the wizard statue.
他们本会离开商店，就在离开时，德怀特把巫师雕像砸碎了。

1324
00:58:18.670 --> 00:58:20.770
And Jim and Andy are like, what are you doing?
然后吉姆和安迪就问，你在干什么？

1325
00:58:20.990 --> 00:58:24.930
And he pries the crystal out of the wizard's hand.
接着他从巫师手里撬出了那颗水晶。

1326
00:58:24.930 --> 00:58:27.410
And he's like, you think I was here for this wizard?
他说，你们以为我是为了这个巫师才来的吗？

1327
00:58:27.590 --> 00:58:28.810
It's the crystal.
是为了这颗水晶。

1328
00:58:31.490 --> 00:58:33.490
Why do I remember that scene?
为什么我会记得那个场景？

1329
00:58:33.490 --> 00:58:35.490
I wasn't there when they shot it.
他们拍摄的时候我并不在场。

1330
00:58:35.490 --> 00:58:39.810
Is it just, like, one of those moments when something was so funny to me at a table read
难道是因为在剧本围读的时候，那一幕对我来说太好笑了，

1331
00:58:39.810 --> 00:58:41.950
that I've never forgotten it?
以至于我一直没忘？

1332
00:58:42.030 --> 00:58:42.170
Yeah.
是啊。

1333
00:58:42.170 --> 00:58:43.210
Because I remember that.
因为我确实记得。

1334
00:58:43.410 --> 00:58:46.130
Dwight had it out for the wizard and stole his crystal.
德怀特就是冲着巫师去的，还偷走了他的水晶。

1335
00:58:46.630 --> 00:58:48.290
I wish we would have kept that in.
真希望我们当时把它留下了。

1336
00:58:48.490 --> 00:58:50.550
It's in the deleted scenes on the DVD.
它在DVD的删减片段里。

1337
00:58:50.550 --> 00:58:51.470
It's really funny.
真的很有趣。

1338
00:58:51.770 --> 00:58:56.990
I guess we should talk about what happened between Michael and Toby after their session
我想我们该聊聊迈克尔和托比在咨询结束后发生了什么，

1339
00:58:56.990 --> 00:58:59.270
ended so abruptly with the double bird.
当时咨询因为那个“双中指”手势戛然而止。

1340
00:58:59.590 --> 00:58:59.950
Yeah.
对。

1341
00:59:00.130 --> 00:59:02.770
Toby just gives Michael the forums and is like, you fill him out.
托比直接把表格扔给迈克尔说，你自己填吧。

1342
00:59:02.770 --> 00:59:05.430
Say you completed the counseling, turn him in.
就说你完成了咨询，然后交上去。

1343
00:59:05.510 --> 00:59:05.970
I don't care.
我不在乎。

1344
00:59:06.190 --> 00:59:06.910
He's done with it.
他已经受够了。

1345
00:59:07.030 --> 00:59:10.270
But I guess Michael accidentally checked off severe.
但我猜迈克尔不小心勾选了“严重”。

1346
00:59:10.710 --> 00:59:12.570
He didn't read the foruMs.
他根本没看表格。

1347
00:59:12.770 --> 00:59:12.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1348
00:59:13.090 --> 00:59:15.590
He said that he was severe in all categories.
他勾选了自己在所有类别中都很严重。

1349
00:59:16.150 --> 00:59:21.390
And Gabe is like, wow, is this really how you feel about Michael after your counseling?
然后盖博就说，哇，咨询之后你对迈克尔的评价真的这么糟糕吗？

1350
00:59:21.750 --> 00:59:23.170
And Toby's like, yeah.
托比就说，没错。

1351
00:59:23.970 --> 00:59:24.670
Guess what?
猜猜怎么着？

1352
00:59:24.790 --> 00:59:26.450
This is going to lead to more counseling.
这又要导致更多的心理辅导了。

1353
00:59:26.930 --> 00:59:27.130
Yeah.
是啊。

1354
00:59:28.610 --> 00:59:30.090
Michael is so mad.
迈克尔太生气了。

1355
00:59:31.710 --> 00:59:33.630
But Toby has an idea.
但托比有个主意。

1356
00:59:33.850 --> 00:59:34.790
He says, you know what?
他说，你知道吗？

1357
00:59:35.030 --> 00:59:36.410
Just forget it.
算了。

1358
00:59:36.570 --> 00:59:38.190
Just get out your notebook.
拿出你的笔记本吧。

1359
00:59:38.210 --> 00:59:39.690
We'll just do some drawings.
我们来画点画。

1360
00:59:40.030 --> 00:59:41.570
We'll just kill the time.
我们就打发下时间。

1361
00:59:41.890 --> 00:59:46.230
Oh, I want you to know, I wish I had kept this prop.
噢，我想让你知道，我真希望我留下了这个道具。

1362
00:59:46.450 --> 00:59:47.450
Me too.
我也是。

1363
00:59:47.450 --> 00:59:49.410
I wish I had it in a frame.
我真希望把它装进相框里。

1364
00:59:49.950 --> 00:59:51.810
Michael draws Dwight and Angela.
迈克尔画了德怀特和安吉拉。

1365
00:59:52.210 --> 00:59:54.670
Angela's taller than Dwight in the drawing.
画里安吉拉比德怀特高。

1366
00:59:54.810 --> 00:59:55.110
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1367
00:59:55.290 --> 00:59:56.930
I wish I had this picture.
我真希望我有这张画。

1368
00:59:57.690 --> 01:00:02.710
I can't believe Toby is still trying to counsel Michael.
真不敢相信托比还在试图给迈克尔做心理辅导。

1369
01:00:02.890 --> 01:00:06.230
He's like, wow, Angela's taller than Dwight.
他就像是，哇，安吉拉比德怀特高。

1370
01:00:06.410 --> 01:00:08.710
I wonder why you drew it that way.
我想知道你为什么会那样画。

1371
01:00:09.110 --> 01:00:11.690
Is that how it seems to you?
在你看来是这样的吗？

1372
01:00:11.790 --> 01:00:12.530
Like, Toby.
我说，托比。

1373
01:00:12.730 --> 01:00:13.190
Toby.
托比。

1374
01:00:13.550 --> 01:00:13.990
Stop.
停下。

1375
01:00:14.290 --> 01:00:15.250
Oh, my goodness.
噢，天哪。

1376
01:00:15.790 --> 01:00:19.910
But the whole episode ends with a Ryan talking head.
但整集结尾是瑞安的采访镜头。

1377
01:00:20.270 --> 01:00:21.290
Yes, it does.
没错，确实是。

1378
01:00:21.290 --> 01:00:25.270
Because it's one of the talking heads that would have been this runner of everyone in
因为那是本该作为贯穿全剧的采访片段之一，让大家在

1379
01:00:25.270 --> 01:00:28.270
the bullpen commenting on Michael's counseling.
办公区评论迈克尔的心理辅导。

1380
01:00:28.690 --> 01:00:30.110
But here's the thing.
但问题是。

1381
01:00:30.450 --> 01:00:34.450
Is it a talking head or is it a series of talking heads?
那是一个采访镜头，还是一系列采访镜头？

1382
01:00:35.290 --> 01:00:38.270
We had a fan question from Joshua P.
我们收到一个来自辛辛那提的乔舒亚·P.

1383
01:00:38.530 --> 01:00:42.930
in Cincinnati and many others who would like to know when Ryan
以及许多其他粉丝的问题，他们想知道当瑞安

1384
01:00:42.930 --> 01:00:49.990
lists off all of these various thoughts on therapy and then at the end says, I don't know, just use the
列举出所有关于治疗的想法，最后说“我不知道，选最好的那个用吧”时，这些是写在剧本里的，还是即兴发挥的备选台词，然后被剪辑成了

1385
01:00:49.990 --> 01:00:56.410
best one, were those scripted or were they candy bag alts and then they just stitched them together as
一个笑话？

1386
01:00:56.410 --> 01:00:57.030
one joke?
安吉拉，我真的很感谢这位粉丝的问题，因为还记得在《尼亚加拉》那一集里，他们给德怀特拍了一堆

1387
01:00:57.250 --> 01:01:04.310
I really appreciate this fan question, Angela, because remember in Niagara, they had a bunch
关于他那个肉类生意的备选台词吗？

1388
01:01:04.310 --> 01:01:08.890
of candy bag alts for Dwight about his, like, meat business?
是的，他们把那些全剪成了一个片段。

1389
01:01:09.150 --> 01:01:10.990
Yes, and they made them all one.
没错。

1390
01:01:10.990 --> 01:01:11.470
Yes.
是的。

1391
01:01:11.710 --> 01:01:12.690
By accident.
那是意外。

1392
01:01:12.930 --> 01:01:13.130
Yes.
是的。

1393
01:01:13.130 --> 01:01:14.650
And they didn't catch it until editing.
而且直到剪辑时他们才发现。

1394
01:01:15.090 --> 01:01:16.370
So what happened here?
那这次是怎么回事？

1395
01:01:16.550 --> 01:01:21.010
I want you to know, I went to the shooting draft and this is one complete talking head.
我想让你知道，我查了拍摄剧本，这是一个完整的采访镜头。

1396
01:01:21.170 --> 01:01:23.030
It's not a bunch of candy bag alts.
它不是一堆备选台词拼凑的。

1397
01:01:23.150 --> 01:01:24.590
It's one talking head.
它就是一个采访镜头。

1398
01:01:24.870 --> 01:01:26.410
BJ read it as scripted.
BJ是照着剧本念的。

1399
01:01:26.590 --> 01:01:31.130
And the last line of this talking head is, I don't know, just use the best one.
而且这个采访镜头的最后一句就是，“我不知道，选最好的那个用吧”。

1400
01:01:31.970 --> 01:01:34.930
Because Ryan is now savvy with the camera crew, right?
因为瑞安现在很懂怎么应付摄像组了，对吧？

1401
01:01:34.930 --> 01:01:35.450
He is.
确实是。

1402
01:01:35.510 --> 01:01:36.610
He knows they're going to edit.
他知道他们会剪辑的。

1403
01:01:36.890 --> 01:01:41.770
He's, you know, he's going through his suspenders and orange watch phase and his glasses
他现在正处于那种背带、橙色手表和眼镜的阶段，还有他的软呢帽。

1404
01:01:41.770 --> 01:01:43.170
and his fedora hat.
还有他的软呢帽。

1405
01:01:43.470 --> 01:01:44.590
He's savvy now.
他现在很精明了。

1406
01:01:44.730 --> 01:01:45.230
He is.
确实是。

1407
01:01:45.350 --> 01:01:50.310
I mean, listen, when we did the lip dub, he knew, I'm going to use this as an opportunity
我是说，听着，当我们做对口型视频的时候，他就知道，我要利用这个机会

1408
01:01:50.310 --> 01:01:51.210
to advertise.
做广告。

1409
01:01:51.530 --> 01:01:51.950
That's right.
没错。

1410
01:01:51.950 --> 01:01:52.590
For Woof.
为Woof做广告。

1411
01:01:52.970 --> 01:01:53.310
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

